{:db/id 17592186124473 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id 17592186124284 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffd143c8-a993-5d0b-85a5-821d6482ae60" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intervals on Which a Function is Invertible Given Its Graph"}] :question/id #uuid "b6722faa-6069-59c1-8861-75b8207b0a90" :question/math-academy-id "e-3962" :question/problem "![](images/d9/d965e0b1087ad45206dd9259c963609f556bf5803af47ab18006bf40dffb2557.png)\n\n     \n\nOn which of the following intervals is the function $f(x)$ (shown above) invertible?\n\n- $(-3,-1]$\n\n- $(0,4]$\n\n- $[-2,2)$" :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.   \n\n- The given function is invertible on the interval $x\\in (-3,-1].$  Indeed, any horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/24/245484a6a77160a5f5892738a7e1f8e488f6df8e4ba990bbc94ae964c3305525.png)\n\n- The given function is **not** invertible on the intervals $(0,4]$ and $[-2,2)$ because some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](images/47/4737a1460e1abd4edc200404407fef10761f038d9a29e52ba0f8c3e8c69bb93f.png)\n\n          \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I  only\"."} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffd143c8-a993-5d0b-85a5-821d6482ae60" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id 17592186124951 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffd143c8-a993-5d0b-85a5-821d6482ae60" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intervals on Which a Function is Invertible Given Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a4b078b7-f5a3-5e10-8da4-739f031e9cbe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186438214} {:answer/id #uuid "8c292220-45e3-5b72-bba6-cb8a5c0646b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186438215}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c292220-45e3-5b72-bba6-cb8a5c0646b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186438215} :answer-field/id #uuid "251d1017-18ef-5bc9-9883-11eca3e38d83" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186439136} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48ad9111-5ff9-5808-834a-73627abed3d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186438216} {:answer/id #uuid "29672cf9-dfff-5490-ae19-b79923580048" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186438217}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "29672cf9-dfff-5490-ae19-b79923580048" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186438217} :answer-field/id #uuid "02d06f78-7466-5d54-950d-cb989daacc0e" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186439137} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fbe0bd4f-6a4d-525e-ac35-a1868f919e0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186438218} {:answer/id #uuid "00a2f1ae-0f2a-55b3-bef4-eabad652d111" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186438219}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fbe0bd4f-6a4d-525e-ac35-a1868f919e0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186438218} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c704ed7-9a63-5c1b-90d0-bdb2e302d80f" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186439138}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b8099f21-9137-5121-a075-a61a4c5ae84b" :question/math-academy-id "q-36039" :question/problem "![](images/93/936cea1e20ef7bbc1eb66acf9dd564c61476f5bb68ee05e553b00aaf3f970dc3.png)\n\nOn which of the following intervals is the function $f(x)$ (shown above) invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x\\in [-4,0]$\n\n- **II.** $x\\in (-4,-2]$\n\n- **III.** $x\\in (-3,1)$" :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.  \n\n- The given function is invertible on each of the intervals $x\\in [-4,0]$ and $x\\in (-4,-2].$ Indeed, any horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/a4/a4499c2d4995c09b9ab6f8852cc2982f415f1650d65429c86df83800344106f4.png)\n\n- The given function is **not** invertible on the interval $x\\in (-3,1]$  because some lines will intersect the curve at more than one point.\n\n![](images/cb/cb0a462b3af10d15bb586f127baac45a74eecd5dc19848bda23664e75de968a4.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"."} {:db/id 17592186125021 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffd143c8-a993-5d0b-85a5-821d6482ae60" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intervals on Which a Function is Invertible Given Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "78aca4cb-e874-5654-89d1-3d26d0e9075a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186438248} {:answer/id #uuid "56ebc0ee-62bb-5743-905c-8d3b1f4543aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186438249}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "56ebc0ee-62bb-5743-905c-8d3b1f4543aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186438249} :answer-field/id #uuid "c4850d87-ba31-5f2e-a2c9-896106eec279" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186439153} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3dae7370-d996-56fe-936b-343de836684b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186438250} {:answer/id #uuid "e2fe8981-13df-58ff-ab19-42ab217c7691" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186438251}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3dae7370-d996-56fe-936b-343de836684b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186438250} :answer-field/id #uuid "565ecd30-91cd-5296-867d-ca7a470f2b8a" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186439154} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0404cc11-e4d5-5e27-b15b-f2c82d4a30c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186438252} {:answer/id #uuid "8fdb23e5-d163-5ce9-8bf0-091f9dbf30d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186438253}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0404cc11-e4d5-5e27-b15b-f2c82d4a30c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186438252} :answer-field/id #uuid "3b827e24-6b4c-5696-943d-0313a9d735b6" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186439155}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e891cfb3-f978-5b44-b8bf-4d4f9f71b503" :question/math-academy-id "q-36941" :question/problem "![](images/3c/3cbdac583a4cdf1b5eb761892934516a0b4edd1487bd402ae0014859c4a0ad53.png)\n\nOn which of the following intervals is the function $f(x)$ (shown above) invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x\\in (-2,0]$\n\n- **II.** $x\\in (-2,2]$\n\n- **III.** $x\\in [-4,-2]\\cup [2,4]$" :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.\n\n- The given function is invertible on the interval $x\\in (-2,0].$ Indeed, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/d7/d7c6e8d314483ad67e89ce5d4675b7af27fa08c88a4ed9d95eed9ad2a4da51cc.png)\n\n- The given function is **not** invertible on the intervals $x\\in (-2,2]$ and $x\\in [-4,-2]\\cup [2,4]$ because some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](images/ce/cee829f7e3d5f32b0acb54cb5c40406d8391d2a2967c68df0c1f5e1cae87d729.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"."} {:db/id 17592186244150 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffd143c8-a993-5d0b-85a5-821d6482ae60" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intervals on Which a Function is Invertible Given Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e7979d09-acc1-57e7-ad97-48330dcf92c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186437534} {:answer/id #uuid "ddb2c6be-faa3-57d6-b152-c27d364876ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186437535}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e7979d09-acc1-57e7-ad97-48330dcf92c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186437534} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ea2ff4f-a861-5561-9d03-05dfc604dd70" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186438796} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "41a9d17d-4814-590e-9cbe-d74bc2c4dcee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186437536} {:answer/id #uuid "29831667-6916-5406-9a77-7bf3fe4d3659" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186437537}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "41a9d17d-4814-590e-9cbe-d74bc2c4dcee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186437536} :answer-field/id #uuid "99586748-b897-5c01-a262-9fae3daf4af2" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186438797} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6143220b-4d6c-55a4-9349-70e4e6455698" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186437538} {:answer/id #uuid "6434145f-922b-5b4b-806b-8e094a8b679f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186437539}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6434145f-922b-5b4b-806b-8e094a8b679f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186437539} :answer-field/id #uuid "99e4a5d1-a6e0-55c4-a395-35a8f3acef7b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186438798}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "15f88305-1592-5719-98bf-9e054cd03fe2" :question/math-academy-id "q-108667" :question/problem "![](images/81/811ead4928d2f245235736dce473d121261ea358ca4ff3a0cc8b01bb2e9f3b31.png)\n\nOn which of the following intervals is the function $f(x)$ (shown above) invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x\\in (-3,3)$\n- **II.** $x\\in [1,4]$\n- **III.** $x\\in (-\\infty ,-3]$" :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.\n\n- The given function is invertible on the interval $x\\in (-\\infty ,-3].$ Indeed, any horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/32/32f1ad5bdec30951900a1c30c2996ea040e65880f859c43769faf374db06a2f0.png)\n\n- The given function is **not** invertible on the intervals $x\\in (-3,3)$ and $x\\in [1,4]$ because some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](images/8e/8ed451b24fa83de513f4a1b5c79d39f94add784c6b7265e765a3381e7b03363a.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"."} {:db/id 17592186244151 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffd143c8-a993-5d0b-85a5-821d6482ae60" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intervals on Which a Function is Invertible Given Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "525e1ea4-6bb3-5a33-a72b-5ca54229e233" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186437540} {:answer/id #uuid "5b4ec695-175b-5f77-9f49-01c0df93d480" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186437541}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5b4ec695-175b-5f77-9f49-01c0df93d480" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186437541} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c32b0be-f2c4-536c-a1eb-36fc12e4aebd" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186438799} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9fb25303-ab56-5cdd-bee9-c1f33b59061a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186437542} {:answer/id #uuid "ff43e512-ac4e-56ca-a5ad-fea896204c19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186437543}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9fb25303-ab56-5cdd-bee9-c1f33b59061a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186437542} :answer-field/id #uuid "adc31504-ebca-597a-a993-cdf2c6e69be4" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186438800} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "96691431-68ee-56fb-967b-b1ff482e5a59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186437544} {:answer/id #uuid "7d673f77-1cab-58bc-b439-aa3fac5d152a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186437545}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7d673f77-1cab-58bc-b439-aa3fac5d152a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186437545} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e437179-705a-505d-a1b3-49271e197fe6" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186438801}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "35a0e892-6583-50a3-a3c1-b86c3920f28b" :question/math-academy-id "q-108673" :question/problem "![](images/3d/3db32ea943ff1f457704a29f325a592eb4e1e0e53ee258041d08346bf9da4716.png)\n\nOn which of the following intervals is the function $f(x)$ (shown above) invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x\\in (-2,0]$\n- **II.** $x\\in (-3,0)$\n- **III.** $x\\in (0,2)$" :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test. \n\n- The given function is invertible on the intervals $x\\in (-2,0]$ and $x\\in (0,2).$ Indeed, any horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/46/46e1daf2cb9025b6a736f223fbe168ea32b66302cebea23ca3a2d473e78b77b3.png)\n\n        \n\n- The given function is **not** invertible on the interval $(-3,0)$  because some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](images/d2/d2ed3670f7c67d60c7739ee35d66943b8341b2a49faa97546242609dd39afabc.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"."} {:db/id 17592186244165 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffd143c8-a993-5d0b-85a5-821d6482ae60" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intervals on Which a Function is Invertible Given Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7aba0040-ed79-59d5-8f0c-1da6506dcb09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [-3,5]" :db/id 17592186242260} {:answer/id #uuid "990dc71b-54dd-525d-99c9-150abcb5fde6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [-3,1]\\cup (3,5]" :db/id 17592186242517} {:answer/id #uuid "a34d8087-ba76-52a1-b9de-dc8c243066f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [-3,1)" :db/id 17592186242609} {:answer/id #uuid "bc11acb5-2479-5b6f-8d5c-5023dd267a04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [1,5]" :db/id 17592186242829} {:answer/id #uuid "d159698e-637b-5ec8-b7bd-777c6c74a47b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [0,5]" :db/id 17592186243023}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "990dc71b-54dd-525d-99c9-150abcb5fde6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [-3,1]\\cup (3,5]" :db/id 17592186242517} :answer-field/id #uuid "c24403e2-8bbf-51d7-83c0-df91fa667cef" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186243783}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c8649e7a-85fc-57ea-9a08-e015b963b698" :question/math-academy-id "q-108791" :question/problem "![](images/4f/4fec1c187ae2eaaf40461775425b31d896bdc63bc99233277d6f6bac8949315d.png)\n\nDetermine the largest domain on which the function $f(x)$ (shown above) is invertible." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the domain of our function is $x\\in [-3,5].$ \n\nA function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ does not pass the horizontal line test on the interval $x\\in (1,3).$ In this case, the horizontal line $y=1$ intersects the graph at more than one point.\n\n![](images/eb/eb544795c61be7dd87568e6def10fc907c3554b603c3b344f88ac2a8ff847f8d.png)\n\n- Among the given options, the largest domain on which the function $f(x)$ is invertible is $x\\in [-3,1]\\cup (3,5].$ On this domain, any horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/40/4059a1ad684023640358af6ee38f0967957336578eb93b3299c9c842e7ce108f.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $x\\in [-3,1]\\cup (3,5].$"} {:db/id 17592186244166 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffd143c8-a993-5d0b-85a5-821d6482ae60" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intervals on Which a Function is Invertible Given Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ca8803d-d3a1-5a90-b629-eaffa681a751" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (-2,4)" :db/id 17592186241421} {:answer/id #uuid "748d7234-22b6-51f3-aa22-b25cfd94da75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [0,4]" :db/id 17592186242216} {:answer/id #uuid "75a09077-b272-55f9-9ec5-02e4cb5e59f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in (0,4)" :db/id 17592186242225} {:answer/id #uuid "874dd0bf-adab-5f92-915f-11ce125271a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [-2,0]" :db/id 17592186242365} {:answer/id #uuid "b8117842-6e5d-53d4-bbd5-db19b3700bb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [-2,4]" :db/id 17592186242796}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "748d7234-22b6-51f3-aa22-b25cfd94da75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [0,4]" :db/id 17592186242216} :answer-field/id #uuid "7223ab10-697e-58e6-b5d8-13b63f336aac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186243661}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a8e69af0-0327-53e8-9129-272172fb2aff" :question/math-academy-id "q-108795" :question/problem "![](images/de/def2afaad6d1f74ca3ac8833ed6e35efea1296b324ef5a14c2d9513983a63456.png)\n\nDetermine the largest interval on which the function $f(x)$ (shown above) is invertible." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the domain of our function is $x\\in [-2,4].$\n\nA function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ does not pass the horizontal line test on the interval $x\\in [-2,0].$ In this case, the horizontal line $y=-2$ intersects the graph at more than one point.\n\n![](images/03/033b9e827caf4fc89d4b179c769f5115254c811953f93caf33d0959bfd063235.png)\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is invertible on the interval $x\\in [0,4].$ On this interval, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/4c/4c91aa95131758065b1d8befe7c69895dc51d2f984a04cc8f06932a32e552792.png)\n\nTherefore, the largest interval on which the function is invertible is:\n\n$$\nx\\in [0,4]\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186323736 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffd143c8-a993-5d0b-85a5-821d6482ae60" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intervals on Which a Function is Invertible Given Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f108dd6c-61c1-5717-8270-831f0354507f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186438184} {:answer/id #uuid "c64a7a6a-c767-501b-8788-7c590bc536b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186438185}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c64a7a6a-c767-501b-8788-7c590bc536b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186438185} :answer-field/id #uuid "73b129ee-af9a-5e28-9358-1428d9acd89e" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186439121} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1299406e-f829-5fd4-8425-b85b65f7d4fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186438186} {:answer/id #uuid "eb523abd-ddb9-5635-ac9c-2ff66317cae1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186438187}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1299406e-f829-5fd4-8425-b85b65f7d4fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186438186} :answer-field/id #uuid "926e0c3c-cd97-51cc-9746-082bf755755f" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186439122} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af648e1c-82fc-509a-86a4-bb4d1e1ddc6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186438188} {:answer/id #uuid "820b9e7c-c94e-5f14-8992-67543fc3d809" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186438189}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "820b9e7c-c94e-5f14-8992-67543fc3d809" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186438189} :answer-field/id #uuid "b77279af-afdb-5c4b-87f9-0e122b9f690b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186439123}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "69ab5c8f-74d2-578a-ab14-a3f834908b70" :question/math-academy-id "q-36002" :question/problem "![](images/c5/c51c5a4de562e5a3301ea76afc6af57b459acd4c46e5c65d54afc226d883a137.png)\n\nOn which of the following intervals is the function $f(x)$ (shown above) invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x\\in (-3,0]$\n- **II.** $x\\in (-3,1)$\n- **III.** $x\\in [0,3)$" :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test. \n\n- The given function is invertible on the intervals $x\\in (-3,0]$ and $x\\in [0,3).$ Indeed, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/00/00a80dde24ca012e0282362224c8b63764f5e149a8bfcda9c76ff4eb958fa93a.png)\n\n \n\n- The given function is **not** invertible on the interval $x\\in (-3,1)$  because some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](images/9e/9ea54918e2ef4310b58e9cf8a0c9b1f9757a404d97dbbfd9e5b037af2193f38c.png)\n\n \n\nHence, the correct answer is 'I and III only''."} {:db/id 17592186323737 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffd143c8-a993-5d0b-85a5-821d6482ae60" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intervals on Which a Function is Invertible Given Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e496da34-dbaf-5186-8e70-09599d4e42f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186438190} {:answer/id #uuid "681351b2-3b37-513b-bb0f-7040b33c72b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186438191}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "681351b2-3b37-513b-bb0f-7040b33c72b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186438191} :answer-field/id #uuid "482ac440-f320-503b-99d7-eb74230b2bc9" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186439124} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04eefd7c-a896-59e8-91d0-cbdf4380aedc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186438192} {:answer/id #uuid "dfcd2979-e497-5817-b474-8325f90706bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186438193}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "04eefd7c-a896-59e8-91d0-cbdf4380aedc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186438192} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d241933-0dfc-5f49-ba97-b39545dc4a25" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186439125} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88c808cf-3477-5af3-b1f2-145c26c92a7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186438194} {:answer/id #uuid "8503b8fd-888a-50aa-943d-954d7bdf8c66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186438195}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8503b8fd-888a-50aa-943d-954d7bdf8c66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186438195} :answer-field/id #uuid "4056b817-e800-5678-8e9e-22469e604236" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186439126}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "544516cf-cdec-5de8-af07-1ff7e5be101e" :question/math-academy-id "q-36004" :question/problem "![](images/15/1597ad53471d0d9b44812c5caa31bcb160cfa150d1df9a9314447fa49e62ccff.png)\n\nOn which of the following intervals is the function $f(x)$ (shown above) invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x\\in [-6,0]$\n\n- **II.** $x\\in [-6,4)$\n\n- **III.** $x\\in [4,10)$" :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.  \n\n- The given function is invertible on each of the intervals $x\\in [-6,0]$ and $x\\in [4,10).$ Indeed, any horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/7c/7cb282e3fa66af801ff03816973d5f5f1d0cb41e39d08a8addd27d7aa9c5b9df.png)\n\n      \n\n- The given function is **not** invertible on the interval $[-6,4]$  because some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](images/00/000953609a7b3e13ad09473ead62f96aa895c7f94aa618884e69883595004fd4.png)\n\n \n\n Therefore, the correct answer is \"I  and III only\"."} {:db/id 17592186323739 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffd143c8-a993-5d0b-85a5-821d6482ae60" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intervals on Which a Function is Invertible Given Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c6dd990f-2330-5d0c-81b4-6370f4d92329" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186438196} {:answer/id #uuid "d3d6745b-46d2-5323-8629-40d7481f8ef5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186438197}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d3d6745b-46d2-5323-8629-40d7481f8ef5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186438197} :answer-field/id #uuid "1fa5f1a4-0dd6-545a-95f5-013d457374c6" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186439127} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8f744e7a-172a-583f-b418-720dc54aa6ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186438198} {:answer/id #uuid "37107bf0-d7a1-5dde-a57d-5db8ff5c2424" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186438199}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8f744e7a-172a-583f-b418-720dc54aa6ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186438198} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb7ed940-ad9d-549b-8ff8-c6ed363707ab" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186439128} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65a72c59-feca-5579-98db-917865bf0995" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186438200} {:answer/id #uuid "73492b46-ebe8-5272-ad45-7118928025ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186438201}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "73492b46-ebe8-5272-ad45-7118928025ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186438201} :answer-field/id #uuid "a7aa9bfc-97c1-53ea-b5a1-715f3992c90c" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186