"true" :db/id 17592186438209} :answer-field/id #uuid "0273b980-43eb-564c-872d-0589397d574e" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186439133} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "890e79b7-dfdd-538c-8e9a-7abc3f553b47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186438210} {:answer/id #uuid "2981f923-7ad3-5ee6-93aa-64b271aaa970" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186438211}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2981f923-7ad3-5ee6-93aa-64b271aaa970" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186438211} :answer-field/id #uuid "5568fe44-2db6-5364-963c-2b0dbd971f58" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186439134} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c1bcc67-9524-5941-9eb2-6c123826210d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186438212} {:answer/id #uuid "cfff16d0-eaff-5775-853f-d6b2f96cf631" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186438213}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c1bcc67-9524-5941-9eb2-6c123826210d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186438212} :answer-field/id #uuid "25f018c0-f200-5146-8568-3810e8f2e7b5" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186439135}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d31db013-e3f7-5fe2-aefa-8428da418673" :question/math-academy-id "q-36011" :question/problem "![](images/b0/b02c2e94e144935f0ff96846cd51b5a969fa8f884a7ca1d09abb231b7c945232.png)\n\nOn which of the following intervals is the function $f(x)$ (shown above) invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x\\in (-4,-2)$\n\n- **II.** $x\\in [-2,3]$\n\n- **III.** $x\\in [-3,3]$" :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.  \n\n- The given function is invertible on each of the intervals $x\\in (-4,-2)$ and $x\\in [-2,3].$ Indeed, any horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/53/53fe88780b2ccb7522d2f1baa711162ec99300c2a2d4da29bba9ca532026cd07.png)\n\n- The given function is **not** invertible on  the interval $x\\in [-3,3]$  because some lines will  intersect the curve at more than one point.\n\n![](images/63/63cee4fc05ab17a8e69d9bfae578fa83c24d73e4677065a54a33a25e0871e718.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"."} {:db/id 17592186323747 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffd143c8-a993-5d0b-85a5-821d6482ae60" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intervals on Which a Function is Invertible Given Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2dbc8c33-86dd-598e-8ee7-fa04f2bc7ca3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [-3,4)" :db/id 17592186321504} {:answer/id #uuid "3b34c587-aba0-515e-a326-983fc0c9bb25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [1,4]" :db/id 17592186321602} {:answer/id #uuid "8b61890c-a1b7-5b5d-ab2c-68b1c461cf55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [-3,1]" :db/id 17592186322259} {:answer/id #uuid "c42fd510-9a4e-5f4a-8ea1-cce741552a32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [-3,4]" :db/id 17592186322670} {:answer/id #uuid "fed6c880-f715-5a34-9e47-e4d3b005ddd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [-3,0]" :db/id 17592186323158}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b61890c-a1b7-5b5d-ab2c-68b1c461cf55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\in [-3,1]" :db/id 17592186322259} :answer-field/id #uuid "bcfb24cc-9668-58dd-abc6-31788a668fce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186323537}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6425603b-0808-58ba-b2d2-92cbdbcccb68" :question/math-academy-id "q-36061" :question/problem "![](images/4d/4d4353286b5d1668d2a67539db8b1fd27227872b1f5a2eaa5fd6015716f255b0.png)\n\nDetermine the largest interval on which the function $f(x)$ (shown above) is invertible." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the domain of our function is $x\\in [-3,4).$\n\nA function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ does not pass the horizontal line test on the interval $x\\in [1,4).$ In this case, the horizontal line $y=-1$ intersects the graph at more than one point.\n\n![](images/a7/a709558673202ef4a7835dcea6e23b7ec5b13684272c56023058223c01fb8061.png)\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is invertible on the interval $x\\in [-3,1].$ On this interval, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/5a/5a65e71f571e9510580ba5fe105a6eac48acfe4564c5a6bf76371c2bf09ff651.png)\n\nTherefore, the largest interval on which the function is invertible is:\n\n$$\nx\\in [-3,1]\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186323749 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffd143c8-a993-5d0b-85a5-821d6482ae60" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intervals on Which a Function is Invertible Given Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "efc69b98-00eb-5840-b90d-c96ba4931e4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186438228} {:answer/id #uuid "4ccd2d26-a281-5b97-9b06-263136be07dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186438229}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4ccd2d26-a281-5b97-9b06-263136be07dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186438229} :answer-field/id #uuid "559a6aac-97fe-50a0-8beb-d1323671d7f8" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186439143} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40a97abe-d55d-5007-b4fd-6937cc34e17a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186438230} {:answer/id #uuid "b173d1e1-4b30-5d88-8de6-73fd6e00131b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186438231}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b173d1e1-4b30-5d88-8de6-73fd6e00131b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186438231} :answer-field/id #uuid "6639d61d-bf93-5072-838b-4370ba49c0ed" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186439144} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6fcc16d7-b530-54ef-9b90-9c7275e5931d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186438232} {:answer/id #uuid "8cf0f901-76be-5f84-b0ee-c5cd9c1a5306" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186438233}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6fcc16d7-b530-54ef-9b90-9c7275e5931d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186438232} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f0537b4-3665-5585-a12b-bb1d508ad121" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186439145}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6815ae09-6f05-5b7b-9ca9-f709c3e26769" :question/math-academy-id "q-36066" :question/problem "![](images/e2/e2065775ae6372e8c820b5e2f19f6f105e032dcd37db1e32e04af5bfa6a4faf9.png)\n\nOn which of the following intervals is the function $f(x)$ (shown above) invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x\\in (-3,-2]\\cup (2,4)$\n- **II.** $x\\in (0,2]$\n- **III.** $x\\in [1,4)$" :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test. \n\n- The given function is invertible on the intervals $x\\in (-3,-2]\\cup (2,4)$ and $x\\in (0,2].$ Indeed, any horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/3c/3c5bc724ee29aee7bef2790012bf0e73ce1ed087134213dbad36a670fd136a36.png)\n\n        \n\n- The given function is **not** invertible on the interval $[1,4)$  because some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](images/03/03b9d70513a4ef99b39c9f05d0c0ac803f8e5611d0967015e9c1d9c0f45bd418.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I  and II only\"."} {:db/id 17592186323865 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffd143c8-a993-5d0b-85a5-821d6482ae60" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intervals on Which a Function is Invertible Given Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c89bf3bc-912d-524b-b8c7-166e854b250f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186438242} {:answer/id #uuid "c6255188-de6f-5359-b3ce-b11fa26ffa9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186438243}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c89bf3bc-912d-524b-b8c7-166e854b250f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186438242} :answer-field/id #uuid "35f5bf02-6bde-5643-acf0-85bec1bb3263" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186439150} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c10d5b55-5751-534e-848f-312026170d5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186438244} {:answer/id #uuid "e0e0d146-26cc-5512-87e3-871fc6ff47b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186438245}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e0e0d146-26cc-5512-87e3-871fc6ff47b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186438245} :answer-field/id #uuid "edb61cc5-3d51-546d-9186-fa06d6294e86" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186439151} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af022492-4d4b-5fe8-ace0-066ff89badcc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186438246} {:answer/id #uuid "d1341450-0c68-5e67-bd60-bd2b0eef6a3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186438247}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "af022492-4d4b-5fe8-ace0-066ff89badcc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186438246} :answer-field/id #uuid "781dd2b1-5946-5698-92e6-edc4b9e58172" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186439152}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2b24e31b-6e93-5c8b-93d0-5c6b5852eeb3" :question/math-academy-id "q-36934" :question/problem "![](images/1e/1eccd6630b69558f8a86f8336e9f0e49f37ffb29acf4a3c8f58be34346b4c93c.png)\n\nOn which of the following intervals is the function $f(x)$ (shown above) invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x\\in [-2,0]$\n- **II.** $x\\in (-3,-2]$\n- **III.** $x\\in (-3,-1]$" :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test. \n\n- The given function is **not** invertible on each of the intervals $x\\in [-2,0]$  and $x\\in (-3,-1]$ because some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](images/d8/d8cc826df6fed7a4106539d88ffa8a1fdc0529904497c2d5413f9761acaccd12.png)\n\n        \n\n- The given function is invertible on the interval $x\\in (-3,-2].$ Indeed, any horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/bc/bc00ed8f4bdf03b248dbd9a1651ed073e352d512b830139505fba3b60e05e7e9.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \" II only\"."}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intervals on Which a Function is Invertible Given Its Graph"}
